## SYNOPSIS TOC
Single-crystalline SOM ZIF-67 with highly ordered macro-microporous structure is successfully constructed by saturated solution-based double-solventassisted strategy. SOM ZIF- ${\cdot67}$ is used as a precursor to prepare $_{3}\mathrm{DOM}$ ${\mathrm{CoSe}}_{2}@C$ through selenization at high temperature. The as-derived $3^{\mathrm{DOM}}$ ${\mathrm{CoSe}}_{2}@C$ is composed of $\mathrm{CoSe}_{2}$ nanoparticles uniformly confined in the $\mathrm{3D}$ ordered macroporous carbon skeleton. Benefiting from the unique hierarchical porous structure, $3^{\mathrm{DOM}}\mathrm{CoSe}_{2}@\mathrm{C}$ as a cathode material for AIBs achieves remarkable rate performance and long cycling stability.
